name verbatlas-va2sp
# VA_va2sp.tsv: "Each line contains the ID of a VerbAtlas frame F followed by the selectional preferences of the roles
# in F ... If a role supports multiple selectional preferences, they are separated by a pipe (|). Some frames support
# two types of selectional preferences: Concrete (C) and Abstract (A)." After the frame and the type, a role and its
# preferences, in turn. A preference id (va:0081p) is the key of a row of VA_preference_info, read as the preference
# that row is. What a line says it says together: the frame's role's preferences, of that type. The first line is the
# release's banner.
match VA_va2sp.tsv

tier row by \n
skip 1
names frame type role1 sp1 role2 sp2 role3 sp3 role4 sp4 role5 sp5 role6 sp6 role7 sp7 role8 sp8 role9 sp9 role10 sp10
tier field by \t
part sp* by |

thing row frame
type frame vaframe
refer sp* verbatlas-preference-info
content type role*

together row
# README: "Some frames support two types of selectional preferences: Concrete (C) and Abstract (A).": a value of that
# list, [OBTAIN, A] (Laplace-Engine#32)
value - type
attest row type
# roleN is a value of VerbAtlas's role inventory, the relation of the frame to its selectional preferences
value - role*
relate row role1 to sp1
relate row role2 to sp2
relate row role3 to sp3
relate row role4 to sp4
relate row role5 to sp5
relate row role6 to sp6
relate row role7 to sp7
relate row role8 to sp8
relate row role9 to sp9
relate row role10 to sp10
